{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe plan-review gate (`5fd2`) deliberately EXEMPTS bugs in v1 — a bug has a different shape (reproduction,\nexpected-vs-actual, fix-plan) than a feature plan, and round-4 data showed the plan criteria draw mostly\nplanning-noise on bugs. This epic designs the dedicated bug-review gate. (Spun out of `5fd2`; was follow-on F6.)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A bug-specific criteria set (reproduction, expected-vs-actual, root-cause, regression test) on the three-pass structure.\n- [ ] Validated on real bug tickets across the corpuses; low false-positive vs the plan criteria on bugs.\n- [ ] Reuses the shared review infrastructure (engine, Pass-2/Pass-3, eval seam).\n- [ ] A review gate tuned to bug tickets (reproduction adequacy, root-cause vs symptom, fix-plan soundness,\n- [ ] Bugs are no longer simply skipped: they get an appropriate, low-false-positive review."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007101040560001,"uuid":"681c1baf-6149-4318-ae9a-3817b01b888a"}